  "source": "Ageon AG Drive Pro user manual (Portuguese), table 1 and chapter 5",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "AG Drive Pro – Manual",
      "url": "https://ageon.com.br/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Manual-AG-Drive-Pro-0.5-a-2-cv-xxxx0093V10R2.pdf",
      "accessed": "2026-11-14",
      "sha256": "f42f81ef07a6ba89c4731cf4dfadefd6576fbe3ce3d07e4af9d7f5494bd2592c",
      "note": "linked in issue #442; parameter list (table 1) and chapter 5, Modbus RTU"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Parameter Pnnn is register 5000 + nnn.",
    "Factory serial settings: 9600 baud, no parity (2 stop bits).",
    "Modbus RTU over RS485: functions 03 and 06 on holding registers only, one register per read. The only exception code is 04. A request with a parity error gets no answer.",
    "The manual gives the register number of each parameter but not its scaling. Its read example returns 10 for P011 at its factory 10.0 s.",
    "To run the drive over Modbus set P301 = 4 and P302 = 3; otherwise the command registers answer with exception 4. Parameters can be read and written either way.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
